dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/4, [class.friend]/6-7: a friend function defined in a
class template (a "hidden friend") is a templated entity; its definition
is implicitly instantiated only when it is odr-used.  Nothing here
compares two tree<value> objects with `<'; value has no operator<, so
instantiating that friend's body would be ill-formed.  The front end
instantiated every friend defined in the class together with the class,
failed ("implicit arithmetic conversion not permitted") and reported the
body as dropped.  A friend defined in a class template specialization is
now deferred like a member function of the specialization and
instantiated only when a converted body refers to it.  This is libstdc++'s _Rb_tree (`friend bool operator<(const
_Rb_tree &, const _Rb_tree &) { return std::lexicographical_compare(...); }',
stl_tree.h:1621), instantiated with every std::map / std::set: for a
non-comparable element it drops std::pair's operator< (stl_pair.h:835) and
__gnu_cxx::__ops::_Iter_less_iter::operator() (predefined_ops.h:44) -- 7
cbmc-cpp descs in the round-163 audit.  test_libstdcxx.desc is the
libstdc++ shape (map<string, value>, set<list::iterator, cmp>).
Header-free.  Fails on the round-163 build bin52.
